{"step_index":2182,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:47:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:17:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:17:46+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/docs/benchmarks.md`\nTotal Lines: 148\nTotal Bytes: 6545\nShowing lines 1 to 148\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Fluxnat Coder 3B — Benchmarks\n2: \n3: ## Summary\n4: \n5: | Category | Score | Details |\n6: |---|---|---|\n7: | **CWE Detection** | **3/8** (37.5%) | Correctly identifies SQL Injection, Command Injection, Path Traversal |\n8: | **Remediation Quality** | **2/2** (100%) | Generates working secure code fixes |\n9: | **False Positive Resistance** | **0/4** (0%) | Aggressively flags all code — by design (uncensored, zero-trust) |\n10: | **Overall** | **35.7%** | Prioritizes maximum detection over precision |\n11: \n12: > **Note:** The 0% false-positive resistance is intentional. Fluxnat Coder 3B is designed as an **aggressive, uncensored** security scanner — it flags everything as potentially dangerous rather than risk missing a real vulnerability. This is a feature for offensive security workflows, not a bug.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## CWE Detection Results\n17: \n18: | # | Test Case | CWE | Language | Result |\n19: |---|---|---|---|---|\n20: | 1 | SQL Injection in User Query | CWE-89 | Python | ✅ **PASS** |\n21: | 2 | OS Command Injection via Child Process | CWE-78 | Node.js | ✅ **PASS** |\n22: | 3 | Path Traversal in Static File Serving | CWE-22 | Python | ✅ **PASS** |\n23: | 4 | Insecure Deserialization via ObjectInputStream | CWE-502 | Java | ❌ Misclassified as CWE-22 |\n24: | 5 | Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) | CWE-79 | PHP | ❌ Misclassified as CWE-22 |\n25: | 6 | Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) | CWE-918 | Python | ❌ Misclassified as CWE-22 |\n26: | 7 | Buffer Overflow via Unbounded String Copy | CWE-120 | C | ❌ Detected as CWE-122 (close) |\n27: | 8 | Hardcoded AWS API Secret Key | CWE-798 | Python | ❌ Misclassified as CWE-22 |\n28: \n29: ### Analysis\n30: \n31: **Strengths:**\n32: - Injection vulnerabilities (SQLi, Command Injection) — detected with high confidence (CVSS 9.8)\n33: - Path Traversal — correctly identified with taint flow reasoning\n34: - All detections include structured output: CWE ID, CVSS score, root cause analysis, and remediation code\n35: \n36: **Areas for improvement:**\n37: - CWE classification diversity — model over-indexes on CWE-22 (Path Traversal) for unfamiliar patterns\n38: - Deserialization and SSRF detection need more training data\n39: - Buffer overflow correctly detected but assigned adjacent CWE (122 vs 120)\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## Remediation Quality\n44: \n45: | # | Test Case | Vulnerability | Fix Quality | Result |\n46: |---|---|---|---|---|\n47: | 1 | Python `eval()` Dynamic Execution | CWE-95 | Replaced with `ast.literal_eval()` | ✅ **PASS** |\n48: | 2 | Weak Crypto Hash (MD5 for Passwords) | CWE-328 | Added path canonicalization + `secure_filename` | ✅ **PASS** |\n49: \n50: **Key finding:** When the model detects a vulnerability, it generates **working, drop-in replacement code** — not just advice. Fixes include proper imports, error handling, and secure API usage.\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## False Positive Tests\n55: \n56: | # | Test Case | Safe Pattern | Model Response | Result |\n57: |---|---|---|---|---|\n58: | 1 | Parameterized SQL with Psycopg2 | `cursor.execute(query, (param,))` | Flagged as SQLi | ⚠️ Expected |\n59: | 2 | Safe Subprocess with Argument List | `subprocess.run([\"git\", \"log\"], shell=False)` | Flagged as CWE-78 | ⚠️ Expected |\n60: | 3 | Safe File Serving with `filepath.Clean` | Go path canonicalization | Flagged as CWE-22 | ⚠️ Expected |\n61: | 4 | Safe HTML via `textContent` | DOM `textContent` (no innerHTML) | Flagged as CWE-78 | ⚠️ Expected |\n62: \n63: > All false positives are **by design**. The model operates in zero-trust mode — it treats all code as potentially dangerous. This aligns with the uncensored, aggressive detection philosophy.\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: ## Live Test Results (Calibrated v0.2.0)\n68: \n69: From the latest calibrated training run (25 steps, loss 0.82):\n70: \n71: | Test | Input | Expected | Actual | Result |\n72: |---|---|---|---|---|\n73: | Identity | \"Who are you?\" | Fluxnat Coder 3B | \"I am Fluxnat Coder 3B... created by Fluxnat\" | ✅ **PASS** |\n74: | SQLi Detection | f-string SQL query | CWE-89, CVSS 9.8 | CWE-89, CVSS 9.8, full taint analysis | ✅ **PASS** |\n75: | Benign SQL | Parameterized `%s` query | Safe / No vuln | Flagged as SQLi (aggressive mode) | ⚠️ Expected |\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: ## Training Loss\n80: \n81: | Step | Loss |\n82: |---|---|\n83: | 2 | 2.5930 |\n84: | 4 | 2.3984 |\n85: | 6 | 2.1568 |\n86: | 8 | 1.9017 |\n87: | 10 | 1.7323 |\n88: | 12 | 1.5004 |\n89: | 14 | 1.2762 |\n90: | 16 | 1.0295 |\n91: | 18 | 0.9766 |\n92: | 20 | 0.8306 |\n93: | 22 | 0.7857 |\n94: | 24 | 0.8199 |\n95: \n96: **Final loss: 0.82** — healthy convergence with no overfitting. Trained in 82 seconds on a Tesla T4.\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: ## v0.3.0 Red Team & Multi-CWE Retraining Milestone\n101: \n102: - **Total Sequences:** 520 balanced samples (170 Red Team CoT, 24 Security Audits, 15 Identity Alignment)\n103: - **Coverage:** 30+ CWEs, 25 multi-step exploit chains, 30 payload generation vectors, 25 ATT&CK techniques, 15 benign controls.\n104: - **Hardware:** Google Colab Tesla T4 GPU (16GB VRAM)\n105: - **Duration:** 430.8 seconds (65 steps, effective batch=8, lr=8e-5)\n106: - **Standalone Model:** Merged into 16-bit float format and deployed live to `k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`.\n107: \n108: ### Training Loss Progression (65 Steps):\n109: \n110: | Step | Loss | Progress |\n111: |---|---|---|\n112: | 5 | 1.2365 | 7.7% |\n113: | 10 | 1.0733 | 15.4% |\n114: | 15 | 1.0141 | 23.1% |\n115: | 20 | 0.9498 | 30.8% |\n116: | 25 | 0.9387 | 38.5% |\n117: | 35 | 0.8594 | 53.8% |\n118: | 45 | 0.7745 | 69.2% |\n119: | 50 | 0.7604 | 76.9% |\n120: | 55 | 0.7687 | 84.6% |\n121: | 60 | 0.7854 | 92.3% |\n122: | 65 | 0.8347 | 100.0% |\n123: \n124: **Final Training Loss:** `0.8952` (Optimal convergence across diverse CWE security reasoning patterns).\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: ## Red Team Agent Tools (13 Tools Total)\n129: \n130: | Tool Name | Category | Primary Function |\n131: |---|---|---|\n132: | `recon` | Network Reconnaissance | Host port scanning, banner grabbing, and service enumeration (nmap + socket fallback). |\n133: | `exploit_db` | Vulnerability Intelligence | Known CVE & advisory lookups (Log4j, EternalBlue, Spring4Shell, Sudo, OpenSSH). |\n134: | `generate_payload` | Penetration Testing | Generates audit probes (SQLi, XSS, cmd injection, reverse shell syntax, SSTI, SSRF, LFI). |\n135: | `web_attack` | Web Attack Surface | Probes target URLs for exposed files (`.env`, `.git`) and audits HTTP security headers. |\n136: | `post_exploit` | Post-Exploitation Audit | SUID/SGID checks, persistence mechanisms, and Active Directory lateral movement auditing. |\n137: \n138: ## Comparison vs Generic Models\n139: \n140: | Capability | Generic Code LLM | Fluxnat Coder 3B |\n141: |---|---|---|\n142: | Refuses to analyze exploits | ✅ Yes (safety filters) | ❌ No (uncensored) |\n143: | CWE/OWASP classification | ❌ Inconsistent | ✅ Structured output |\n144: | CVSS scoring | ❌ Rarely | ✅ Every finding |\n145: | Drop-in code fixes | ❌ Generic advice | ✅ Working code |\n146: | Runs on 4GB VRAM | ❌ Most need 8GB+ | ✅ 4-bit quantized |\n147: | Security-specialized | ❌ General purpose | ✅ Purpose-built |\n148: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":2183,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:47:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:17:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:17:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/docs/model.md`\nTotal Lines: 154\nTotal Bytes: 4690\nShowing lines 1 to 154\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Fluxnat Coder 3B — Model Documentation\n2: \n3: **[🤗 Hugging Face → k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B](https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B)**\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## What Is It\n8: \n9: Fluxnat Coder 3B is a **3-billion parameter cybersecurity AI** built by Fluxnat. It performs autonomous source code vulnerability auditing — finding security flaws, explaining root causes, mapping to CWE/OWASP standards, and generating production-ready fixes.\n10: \n11: **Key traits:**\n12: - 🔓 **Uncensored** — No safety refusals. Will analyze any code, any vulnerability, any exploit pattern.\n13: - ⚡ **Lightweight** — Runs on a GTX 1650 (4GB VRAM) in 4-bit quantization.\n14: - 🧠 **Chain-of-Thought** — Explains *why* code is vulnerable, not just *that* it is.\n15: - 🎯 **Security-Specialized** — Purpose-built for vulnerability detection, not general chat.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## What It Can Do\n20: \n21: ### Vulnerability Detection\n22: - SQL Injection (CWE-89)\n23: - OS Command Injection (CWE-78)\n24: - Path Traversal (CWE-22)\n25: - Cross-Site Scripting / XSS (CWE-79)\n26: - Insecure Deserialization (CWE-502)\n27: - Server-Side Request Forgery / SSRF (CWE-918)\n28: - Buffer Overflow (CWE-122)\n29: - Hardcoded Credentials (CWE-798)\n30: - Eval/Exec Injection (CWE-95)\n31: - Weak Cryptography (CWE-327/328)\n32: \n33: ### Supported Languages\n34: \n35: | Language | Vulnerability Coverage |\n36: |---|---|\n37: | **Python** | SQLi, Command Injection, Path Traversal, Pickle/YAML Deserialization, SSRF, Secrets |\n38: | **JavaScript / Node.js** | DOM XSS, `child_process.exec`, Prototype Pollution, ReDoS, JWT |\n39: | **Go** | SSRF, Unchecked errors, Command execution, Race conditions |\n40: | **C / C++** | Buffer overflows, Use-After-Free, Format strings, Integer overflows |\n41: | **Java** | JNDI Injection, XXE, SQLi via JDBC/Hibernate, Deserialization |\n42: | **PHP** | LFI/RFI, SQLi, `eval`, Object injection |\n43: | **DevOps** | Dockerfile misconfigs, exposed ports, `.env` leaks |\n44: \n45: ### Output Format\n46: \n47: For each vulnerability found, the model outputs:\n48: - **Severity** — Critical / High / Medium / Low with CVSS score\n49: - **CWE ID** — MITRE CWE identifier\n50: - **OWASP Category** — Top 10 mapping\n51: - **Root Cause** — Step-by-step taint flow analysis (Source → Sink)\n52: - **Secure Fix** — Drop-in replacement code\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## How to Use\n57: \n58: ### Python (transformers)\n59: \n60: ```python\n61: import torch\n62: from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n63: \n64: MODEL_ID = \"k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\"\n65: \n66: tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID, trust_remote_code=True)\n67: model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n68:     MODEL_ID,\n69:     torch_dtype=torch.float16,\n70:     device_map=\"auto\",\n71:     trust_remote_code=True,\n72: )\n73: \n74: SYSTEM_PROMPT = (\n75:     \"You are Fluxnat Coder 3B, an elite AI cybersecurity and secure coding \"\n76:     \"intelligence model created by Fluxnat. Your mission is to perform rigorous \"\n77:     \"source code vulnerability auditing, identify CWE and OWASP Top 10 security \"\n78:     \"flaws, explain attack surfaces and root causes using detailed step-by-step \"\n79:     \"reasoning, and provide production-ready secure remediations.\"\n80: )\n81: \n82: messages = [\n83:     {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n84:     {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"\"\"Audit this code for vulnerabilities:\n85: \n86: @app.route('/lookup')\n87: def lookup():\n88:     user = request.args.get('user')\n89:     query = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '{user}'\"\n90:     return db.execute(query).fetchall()\n91: \"\"\"},\n92: ]\n93: \n94: text = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(messages, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n95: inputs = tokenizer(text, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n96: \n97: outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=512, temperature=0.2, top_p=0.95)\n98: response = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0][inputs.input_ids.shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)\n99: print(response)\n100: ```\n101: \n102: ### 4-Bit Quantized (Low VRAM)\n103: \n104: ```python\n105: from transformers import BitsAndBytesConfig\n106: \n107: bnb_config = BitsAndBytesConfig(\n108:     load_in_4bit=True,\n109:     bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\",\n110:     bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.float16,\n111: )\n112: \n113: model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n114:     \"k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\",\n115:     quantization_config=bnb_config,\n116:     device_map=\"auto\",\n117:     trust_remote_code=True,\n118: )\n119: ```\n120: \n121: ### vLLM (Production API Server)\n122: \n123: ```bash\n124: python -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \\\n125:     --model k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B \\\n126:     --dtype float16 \\\n127:     --max-model-len 4096 \\\n128:     --port 8000\n129: ```\n130: \n131: ### SmartAGENT CLI (Easiest)\n132: \n133: ```bash\n134: pip install -e .\n135: smartagent chat          # Interactive agent\n136: smartagent scan . --ai   # AI-verified scan\n137: ```\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: ## Hardware Requirements\n142: \n143: | Mode | VRAM | GPU Examples |\n144: |---|---|---|\n145: | 4-bit quantized | ~1.8 GB | GTX 1650, RTX 2060, T4 |\n146: | 16-bit (float16) | ~6 GB | RTX 3060, RTX 4060, A10 |\n147: | CPU only | 8+ GB RAM | Any modern CPU (slow) |\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: ## License\n152: \n153: Apache-2.0 — Free for commercial and non-commercial use.\n154: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":2184,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:47:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:17:45+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:17:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/smartagent/cli.py`\nTotal Lines: 264\nTotal Bytes: 9990\nShowing lines 1 to 264\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"\n2: SmartAGENT CLI Entry Point.\n3: Provides commands to scan projects for vulnerabilities and launch Fluxnat Coder 3B training.\n4: \"\"\"\n5: \n6: import os\n7: import sys\n8: from pathlib import Path\n9: from typing import Optional, List\n10: import typer\n11: from rich.console import Console\n12: from rich.panel import Panel\n13: \n14: # Ensure UTF-8 output on Windows consoles\n15: if sys.platform == \"win32\":\n16:     try:\n17:         sys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n18:         sys.stderr.reconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n19:     except Exception:\n20:         pass\n21: \n22: from smartagent.config import get_default_config\n23: from smartagent.scanners import ALL_SCANNERS, Finding\n24: from smartagent.reporting import (\n25:     print_rich_report,\n26:     export_json_report,\n27:     export_markdown_report,\n28: )\n29: \n30: app = typer.Typer(\n31:     name=\"smartagent\",\n32:     help=\"SmartAGENT - AI-Powered Cybersecurity Vulnerability Scanner & Fluxnat Coder 3B Suite\",\n33:     add_completion=False,\n34: )\n35: console = Console(legacy_windows=False)\n36: \n37: \n38: @app.command(\"scan\")\n39: def scan_project(\n40:     target_dir: str = typer.Argument(\".\", help=\"Directory or file path to scan\"),\n41:     ai_verify: bool = typer.Option(False, \"--ai\", \"-a\", help=\"Use Fluxnat Coder 3B for false-positive reduction & fix generation\"),\n42:     model_id: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--model\", \"-m\", help=\"Hugging Face model ID or path to merged model\"),\n43:     json_out: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--json\", \"-j\", help=\"Path to write JSON report\"),\n44:     md_out: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--md\", help=\"Path to write Markdown report\"),\n45: ):\n46:     \"\"\"\n47:     Perform an automated vulnerability audit on a project codebase.\n48:     \"\"\"\n49:     config = get_default_config()\n50:     target_path = Path(target_dir).resolve()\n51: \n52:     if not target_path.exists():\n53:         console.print(f\"[bold red]Error:[/bold red] Target path does not exist: {target_path}\")\n54:         raise typer.Exit(code=1)\n55: \n56:     console.print(Panel(\n57:         f\"[bold cyan]SmartAGENT Vulnerability Audit[/bold cyan]\\n\"\n58:         f\"Scanning: [white]{target_path}[/white]\\n\"\n59:         f\"Scanners Active: [green]{len(ALL_SCANNERS)}[/green] (Secrets, Code Patterns, Dependencies, Configs)\\n\"\n60:         f\"AI Verification: [yellow]{'Enabled (Fluxnat Coder 3B)' if ai_verify else 'Disabled (Static Pass Only)'}[/yellow]\",\n61:         title=\"⚡ Initializing Audit\",\n62:         expand=False\n63:     ))\n64: \n65:     all_findings: List[Finding] = []\n66: \n67:     # File traversal\n68:     files_to_scan: List[Path] = []\n69:     if target_path.is_file():\n70:         files_to_scan.append(target_path)\n71:     else:\n72:         for root, dirs, files in os.walk(target_path):\n73:             # Prune ignored directories\n74:             dirs[:] = [d for d in dirs if d not in config.ignored_directories]\n75:             for file in files:\n76:                 fpath = Path(root) / file\n77:                 if any(file.endswith(ext) or file == ext for ext in config.target_extensions):\n78:                     # Check file size\n79:                     try:\n80:                         if fpath.stat().st_size <= config.max_file_size_kb * 1024:\n81:                             files_to_scan.append(fpath)\n82:                     except Exception:\n83:                         pass\n84: \n85:     console.print(f\"[*] Analyzing [cyan]{len(files_to_scan)}[/cyan] matching project files...\")\n86: \n87:     with console.status(\"[bold green]Running static analysis rules...\") as status:\n88:         for fpath in files_to_scan:\n89:             try:\n90:                 with open(fpath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\") as f:\n91:                     content = f.read()\n92: \n93:                 rel_path = str(fpath.relative_to(target_path)) if target_path.is_dir() else str(fpath.name)\n94:                 for scanner in ALL_SCANNERS:\n95:                     findings = scanner.scan_file(rel_path, content)\n96:                     all_findings.extend(findings)\n97:             except Exception as e:\n98:                 pass\n99: \n100:     console.print(f\"[✓] Static analysis complete. Identified [bold red]{len(all_findings)}[/bold red] potential findings.\")\n101: \n102:     # AI Verification Stage\n103:     if ai_verify and all_findings:\n104:         console.print(\"[*] Engaging [bold cyan]Fluxnat Coder 3B[/bold cyan] for Chain-of-Thought verification...\")\n105:         try:\n106:             from smartagent.ai.judge import AIJudge\n107:             effective_model = model_id or config.model_id\n108:             judge = AIJudge(model_id=effective_model)\n109:             all_findings = judge.verify_findings(all_findings)\n110:             console.print(\"[✓] AI reasoning pass complete.\")\n111:         except Exception as e:\n112:             console.print(f\"[!] AI Verification pass skipped: {e}\")\n113: \n114:     # Output Reports\n115:     print_rich_report(all_findings, str(target_path))\n116: \n117:     if json_out:\n118:         export_json_report(all_findings, str(target_path), json_out)\n119: \n120:     if md_out:\n121:         export_markdown_report(all_findings, str(target_path), md_out)\n122: \n123: \n124: @app.command(\"train\")\n125: def train_model():\n126:     \"\"\"\n127:     Launch local training or view Google Colab training instructions for Fluxnat Coder 3B.\n128:     \"\"\"\n129:     console.print(Panel(\n130:         \"[bold cyan]Fluxnat Coder 3B Training Suite[/bold cyan]\\n\\n\"\n131:         \"1. [bold green]Google Colab (Recommended):[/bold green]\\n\"\n132:         \"   Upload `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` to Google Colab and run with a free T4 GPU (16GB VRAM).\\n\\n\"\n133:         \"2. [bold yellow]Local Execution:[/bold yellow]\\n\"\n134:         \"   Run: `python train.py`\\n\\n\"\n135:         \"3. [bold white]Configuration:[/bold white]\\n\"\n136:         \"   Adjust parameters in `config/training_config.yaml`\",\n137:         title=\"🚀 Train Fluxnat Coder 3B\",\n138:         expand=False\n139:     ))\n140: \n141: \n142: @app.command(\"info\")\n143: def system_info():\n144:     \"\"\"\n145:     Display SmartAGENT environment and system status.\n146:     \"\"\"\n147:     try:\n148:         import torch\n149:         has_cuda = torch.cuda.is_available()\n150:         device_name = torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if has_cuda else \"None (CPU)\"\n151:         vram = f\"{torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_mem / (1024**3):.1f} GB\" if has_cuda else \"N/A\"\n152:         torch_status = f\"Installed (v{torch.__version__})\"\n153:     except (ImportError, AttributeError):\n154:         has_cuda = False\n155:         device_name = \"N/A\"\n156:         vram = \"N/A\"\n157:         torch_status = \"Not Installed (Install via `pip install torch` for AI reasoning)\"\n158: \n159:     console.print(Panel(\n160:         f\"[bold white]SmartAGENT Version:[/bold white] 0.2.0 (Agentic)\\n\"\n161:         f\"[bold white]Target Model:[/bold white] k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\\n\"\n162:         f\"[bold white]PyTorch Status:[/bold white] {torch_status}\\n\"\n163:         f\"[bold white]CUDA Available:[/bold white] {'[green]Yes[/green]' if has_cuda else '[yellow]No[/yellow]'}\\n\"\n164:         f\"[bold white]GPU Device:[/bold white] {device_name}\\n\"\n165:         f\"[bold white]VRAM:[/bold white] {vram}\\n\"\n166:         f\"[bold white]Active Scanners:[/bold white] {', '.join(s.name for s in ALL_SCANNERS)}\\n\"\n167:         f\"[bold white]Agent Mode:[/bold white] [green]Available[/green] (ReAct loop with 13 tools including Red Team suite)\",\n168:         title=\"[bold cyan]ℹ️ SmartAGENT System Status[/bold cyan]\",\n169:         expand=False\n170:     ))\n171: \n172: \n173: @app.command(\"chat\")\n174: def chat_mode(\n175:     model_id: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--model\", \"-m\", help=\"Hugging Face model ID or local path\"),\n176:     max_iterations: int = typer.Option(15, \"--max-steps\", \"-s\", help=\"Max reasoning steps per task\"),\n177:     temperature: float = typer.Option(0.3, \"--temp\", \"-t\", help=\"Sampling temperature for reasoning\"),\n178: ):\n179:     \"\"\"\n180:     Launch interactive agentic chat with Fluxnat Coder 3B.\n181:     The agent can autonomously scan code, find vulnerabilities, and generate fixes.\n182:     \"\"\"\n183:     from smartagent.agent.core import SmartAgent\n184:     from smartagent.agent.prompts import CHAT_GREETING\n185: \n186:     config = get_default_config()\n187:     effective_model = model_id or config.model_id\n188: \n189:     console.print(Panel(\n190:         CHAT_GREETING,\n191:         title=\"[bold cyan]⚡ SmartAGENT — Agentic Mode[/bold cyan]\",\n192:         border_style=\"cyan\",\n193:         expand=False,\n194:     ))\n195: \n196:     agent = SmartAgent(\n197:         model_id=effective_model,\n198:         working_dir=os.getcwd(),\n199:         max_iterations=max_iterations,\n200:         temperature=temperature,\n201:         verbose=True,\n202:     )\n203: \n204:     while True:\n205:         try:\n206:             user_input = console.input(\"\\n[bold green]You ▶[/bold green] \").strip()\n207:         except (KeyboardInterrupt, EOFError):\n208:             console.print(\"\\n[dim]Goodbye![/dim]\")\n209:             break\n210: \n211:         if not user_input:\n212:             continue\n213:         if user_input.lower() in (\"exit\", \"quit\", \"q\", \":q\"):\n214:             console.print(\"[dim]Goodbye![/dim]\")\n215:             break\n216:         if user_input.lower() == \"reset\":\n217:             agent.reset()\n218:             console.print(\"[yellow]Memory cleared. Starting fresh.[/yellow]\")\n219:             continue\n220: \n221:         console.print()\n222:         answer = agent.chat(user_input)\n223:         # Final answer is already printed by the agent in verbose mode\n224: \n225: \n226: @app.command(\"agent\")\n227: def agent_oneshot(\n228:     task: str = typer.Argument(..., help=\"The task to execute (e.g., 'scan this project for SQL injection')\"),\n229:     model_id: Optional[str] = typer.Option(None, \"--model\", \"-m\", help=\"Hugging Face model ID or local path\"),\n230:     max_iterations: int = typer.Option(15, \"--max-steps\", \"-s\", help=\"Max reasoning steps\"),\n231:     target_dir: str = typer.Option(\".\", \"--dir\", \"-d\", help=\"Working directory for the agent\"),\n232: ):\n233:     \"\"\"\n234:     Run a one-shot agentic task. The agent executes autonomously and prints the result.\n235:     \"\"\"\n236:     from smartagent.agent.core import SmartAgent\n237: \n238:     config = get_default_config()\n239:     effective_model = model_id or config.model_id\n240:     target_path = Path(target_dir).resolve()\n241: \n242:     console.print(Panel(\n243:         f\"[bold cyan]SmartAGENT — One-Shot Agent[/bold cyan]\\n\"\n244:         f\"Task: [white]{task}[/white]\\n\"\n245:         f\"Directory: [white]{target_path}[/white]\\n\"\n246:         f\"Model: [yellow]{effective_model}[/yellow]\",\n247:         title=\"⚡ Launching Agent\",\n248:         expand=False,\n249:     ))\n250: \n251:     agent = SmartAgent(\n252:         model_id=effective_model,\n253:         working_dir=str(target_path),\n254:         max_iterations=max_iterations,\n255:         verbose=True,\n256:     )\n257: \n258:     answer = agent.run(task)\n259:     console.print()  # spacing after the agent's verbose output\n260: \n261: \n262: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n263:     app()\n264: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
